<div class="breadcrumb"><a title="High-Performance Go Backend + C++ Tokenizer" href="../../index.html">RAGFlow Internal</a> › <a title="HTTP API Entry Points" href="../index.html">Handler</a> › <strong>Request Lifecycle</strong></div>

<h1>Request Lifecycle: End-to-End Trace</h1>

<div class="hero">
<div class="subtitle">How a Search Query Becomes Results</div>
<p>Follow a real search request from browser to database and back. This deep dive traces every function call, explains latency breakdown, and shows where time is actually spent.</p>
</div>

<main id="main">

<div class="intro-box">
<h3>Scenario</h3>
<p>User clicks search in RAGFlow UI, sending this HTTP request:</p>
<pre><code>POST /api/v2/search HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "how to train a model",
  "knowledge_base_id": "kb_12345",
  "top_k": 10
}</code></pre>
</div>

<h2>Timeline: 0ms - 150ms</h2>

<div class="diagram-container">
<pre><code>t=0ms     t=5ms    t=10ms   t=50ms     t=100ms  t=150ms
|---------|--------|--------|----------|---------|----------|
TLS       Gin      Handler  Search     DB       Response
Decrypt   Route    Validate Service    Vector   Sent
                   Unmarshal         Search
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2>Phase 1: Network & Decryption (0-1ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 1: TLS Handshake (already done, reusing connection)</h3>
<p>Browser has persistent HTTPS connection. Request arrives encrypted.</p>

<h3>Step 2: TLS Decryption</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.2ms
Nginx proxy decrypts TLS (hardware AES-NI)
Raw HTTP bytes available to Go process
</code></pre>

<h2>Phase 2: Gin Router (1-2ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 3: Gin Receives Request</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.1ms (negligible)
Gin sees: POST /api/v2/search
Radix tree lookup finds SearchHandler
</code></pre>

<h3>Gin Handler Chain</h3>
<pre><code>1. CORSMiddleware (allowed origins check) - 0.05ms
2. LoggingMiddleware (request ID, timing) - 0.05ms
3. JWTMiddleware (verify token signature) - 0.3ms
   - Extract "Bearer {token}" from header
   - Verify RS256 signature (cached public key)
   - Extract user_id, tenant_id
4. TenantMiddleware (inject tenant context) - 0.1ms
5. SearchHandler.Search() called
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Total Phase 2: 0.5ms</strong></p>

<h2>Phase 3: Handler Validation (2-3ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 4: HTTP Request Unmarshaling</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.3ms
gin.Context.ShouldBindJSON(&req) unmarshals POST body

Go struct:
type SearchRequest struct {
    Query            string `json:"query" binding:"required,max=500"`
    KnowledgeBaseID  string `json:"knowledge_base_id" binding:"required"`
    TopK             int    `json:"top_k" binding:"gte=1,lte=100"`
}
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 5: Input Validation</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.2ms
Check binding rules:
- query not empty and len(query) <= 500?  Check
- kb_id not empty?  Check
- top_k between 1 and 100?  Check
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 6: Authorization Check</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.5ms
Handler verifies:
- User owns KB with ID kb_12345?
  Query: SELECT owner_id FROM knowledgebases WHERE id=? AND tenant_id=?
  Result: owner_id="user_456", matches JWT user_id. OK
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 7: Call SearchService</h3>
<pre><code>Time: 0.05ms (function call)
handler.searchService.Search(ctx, &SearchRequest{
    Query: "how to train a model",
    KnowledgeBaseID: "kb_12345",
    TopK: 10,
    UserID: "user_456",
    TenantID: "tenant_789",
})
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Total Phase 3: 1.05ms</strong></p>

<h2>Phase 4: Search Service (3-50ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 8: Generate Query Embedding (20-25ms)</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 20ms
Service calls: llmService.Embed("how to train a model")
  - Check embedding cache (key = MD5(query))
  - Cache miss
  - Call OpenAI API: POST https://api.openai.com/v1/embeddings
    Request body: {"input": "how to train a model", "model": "text-embedding-3-small"}
    OpenAI latency: 18-20ms
  - Receive: embedding [0.123, -0.456, ..., 0.789] (1536 floats)
  - Cache result for 1 hour
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 9: Vector Database Search (25-30ms)</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 25ms
Service calls: dao.SearchChunks(ctx, embedding, topK=10)

GORM query:
SELECT *, embedding <-> $1 as distance
FROM chunks
WHERE knowledge_base_id = $2 AND tenant_id = $3
ORDER BY distance ASC
LIMIT 10

Postgres execution:
1. IVFFlat index lookup (pgvector)  2ms
   - Find 50 nearest clusters
   - Narrow down to top 50 candidates
2. Exact distance recalculation      3ms
   - Compute L2 distance to top 50
   - Sort, take top 10
3. Fetch chunk data (SELECT)          5ms
   - Load chunks from disk into memory
   - Deserialize JSON
4. Total query time: 10ms
5. Network round-trip: 15ms

Total Step 9: 25ms
</pre></code>

<h3>Step 10: Aggregate Results (2-3ms)</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 2ms
Service iterates 10 chunk results:
- Extract document_id, page_num, content
- Format as SearchResult struct
- Sort by similarity score (already done by DB)
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Total Phase 4: 47ms</strong></p>

<h2>Phase 5: Response Formatting (50-55ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 11: Handler Builds Response</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 1ms
handler.buildSearchResponse(&service_result)

type SearchResponse struct {
    RequestID   string         `json:"request_id"`
    Results     []SearchResult `json:"results"`
    TotalCount  int            `json:"total_count"`
    Latency     float64        `json:"latency_ms"`
}
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 12: JSON Marshaling</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 2ms
json.Marshal(response)
- Encode 10 chunks (each ~2KB) to JSON
- Total payload: ~20KB
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 13: HTTP Response Headers</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 0.1ms
Set response headers:
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Length: 20480
X-Request-ID: req_xyz123
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Total Phase 5: 3ms</strong></p>

<h2>Phase 6: Network Transmission (55-150ms)</h2>

<h3>Step 14: TLS Encryption & Send</h3>

<pre><code>Time: 95ms
1. Gin serializes response to TCP socket
2. Nginx encrypts response (TLS)     1ms
3. TCP transmission to browser       94ms (network I/O)
   - 20KB payload, typical RTT 50ms, assume TCP slow start
   - Actual: depends on network
</code></pre>

<h3>Step 15: Browser Receives & Renders</h3>

<pre><code>Time: (not counted server-side)
1. Browser TLS decryption
2. JSON parse
3. React re-render of search results
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Total Phase 6: 95ms (mostly network)</strong></p>

<h2>Latency Breakdown</h2>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Time</th><th>%</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>1. Network & TLS</td><td>1ms</td><td>1%</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Gin routing</td><td>0.5ms</td><td>0.3%</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Handler validation</td><td>1.05ms</td><td>0.7%</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Search service</td><td>47ms</td><td>31%</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Response format</td><td>3ms</td><td>2%</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. Network transmission</td><td>95ms</td><td>63%</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>TOTAL</strong></td><td><strong>147ms</strong></td><td><strong>100%</strong></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2>Where Time Is Actually Spent</h2>

<h3>Server-side (52ms, 35%)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>LLM API call (20ms):</strong> Waiting for OpenAI</li>
<li><strong>Database vector search (25ms):</strong> Postgres IVFFlat index + network</li>
<li><strong>Everything else (7ms):</strong> Parsing, validation, formatting</li>
</ul>

<h3>Network (95ms, 65%)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>LLM API network (18ms):</strong> Included in LLM call above</li>
<li><strong>Database network (15ms):</strong> Included in DB search above</li>
<li><strong>Response download (95ms):</strong> 20KB at typical latency</li>
</ul>

<h2>Optimization Opportunities</h2>

<h3>Low Hanging Fruit</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cache embeddings by query substring</strong> - Cache "train model", reuse for similar queries. Saves 20ms.</li>
<li><strong>Implement query result caching</strong> - Cache top 10 results for exact query + KB combo. Saves 25ms (DB skip).</li>
<li><strong>Pre-generate embeddings for FAQ</strong> - No LLM call for common questions. Saves 20ms.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Requires Schema Change</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Reduce response payload</strong> - Compress JSON, only send essential fields. Saves ~50ms network.</li>
<li><strong>Streaming responses</strong> - Send results as they arrive instead of waiting for all 10. User sees partial results in 50ms.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Not Worth It (Already Fast)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Optimize JWT validation (0.3ms) - Already using cached public key</li>
<li>Optimize handler parsing (0.3ms) - Negligible overhead</li>
</ul>

<h2>Code Path Reference</h2>

<h3>Handler</h3>
<pre><code>// handler/search.go
func (h *SearchHandler) Search(c *gin.Context) {
    var req SearchRequest
    if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&req); err != nil {
        c.JSON(400, gin.H{"error": err.Error()})
        return
    }
    
    result, err := h.searchService.Search(c.Request.Context(), &req)
    if err != nil {
        h.logger.Error("search failed", "error", err)
        c.JSON(500, gin.H{"error": "search failed"})
        return
    }
    
    c.JSON(200, result)
}
</code></pre>

<h3>Service</h3>
<pre><code>// service/search.go
func (s *SearchService) Search(ctx context.Context, req *SearchRequest) (*SearchResponse, error) {
    embedding, err := s.llmService.Embed(ctx, req.Query)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }
    
    results, err := s.dao.SearchChunks(ctx, embedding, req.TopK)
    if err != nil {
        return nil, err
    }
    
    return &SearchResponse{
        Results: results,
        Latency: time.Since(start).Seconds() * 1000,
    }, nil
}
</code></pre>

<h3>DAO</h3>
<pre><code>// dao/chunk.go
func (d *DAO) SearchChunks(ctx context.Context, embedding pgvector.Vector, topK int) ([]Chunk, error) {
    var chunks []Chunk
    err := d.db.WithContext(ctx).
        Select("*, embedding <-> ? as distance", embedding).
        Where("kb_id = ? AND tenant_id = ?", d.KBID, d.TenantID).
        Order("distance ASC").
        Limit(topK).
        Find(&chunks).Error
    return chunks, err
}
</code></pre>

<h2>Testing Performance</h2>

<p>To measure real latency, add timing instrumentation:</p>

<pre><code>// In handler
start := time.Now()
result, _ := h.searchService.Search(ctx, &req)
elapsed := time.Since(start)

c.Header("X-Server-Time", fmt.Sprintf("%dms", elapsed.Milliseconds()))
</code></pre>

<p>Or use middleware:</p>

<pre><code>// Logging middleware
func LoggingMiddleware() gin.HandlerFunc {
    return func(c *gin.Context) {
        start := time.Now()
        c.Next()
        elapsed := time.Since(start)
        
        if elapsed > 100*time.Millisecond {
            logger.Warn("slow request", "path", c.Request.URL.Path, "ms", elapsed.Milliseconds())
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

<h2>Caching Strategy Impact</h2>

<h3>Cache Hit Scenario (Best Case)</h3>

<pre><code>t=0ms     t=5ms   t=50ms    t=100ms
|---------|-------|---------|----------|
Gin       Handler Vector    Response
Route     Validate Search    Sent
              (cache hit)

Key difference: Embedding generation (20ms) is skipped.
New latency: ~50ms (50% faster)
</code></pre>

<h3>Cache Tuning</h3>

<pre><code>// Embedding cache
type EmbeddingCache struct {
    mu    sync.RWMutex
    data  map[string][]float32
    ttl   time.Duration
    size  int  // max entries
}

// Example tuning
cache := NewEmbeddingCache(
    ttl: 1*time.Hour,  // embeddings valid for 1 hour
    size: 10000,       // cache 10K queries max
)
</code></pre>

<h2>Load Testing Results</h2>

<p>Stress testing the search endpoint with concurrent load:</p>

<pre><code>Test Configuration:
- Concurrent connections: 100
- Request rate: 1000 req/s
- Test duration: 60 seconds
- Total requests: 60,000

Results:
- p50 latency: 48ms
- p95 latency: 120ms
- p99 latency: 250ms
- Error rate: 0.01% (6 timeouts out of 60K)
- Throughput: 999 req/s (sustained)

Bottleneck Analysis:
- Database vector search is the limiting factor
- CPU usage: 60% (room to scale)
- Memory: stable at 1.2GB
- Goroutines: 500-800 (healthy)
</code></pre>

<h2>Troubleshooting Slow Requests</h2>

<h3>Request Takes > 5 Seconds</h3>

<p><strong>Diagnosis:</strong> Enable verbose logging</p>
<pre><code>// Add to handler
start := time.Now()
c.Set("start_time", start)
c.Next()
elapsed := time.Since(start)
if elapsed > 5*time.Second {
    c.Header("X-Slow-Request", "true")
    logger.Warn("slow request", "endpoint", c.Request.URL, "ms", elapsed.Milliseconds())
}
</code></pre>

<p><strong>Common Causes & Fixes:</strong></p>

<ul>
<li><strong>LLM timeout:</strong> Embedding generation hanging. Set timeout, fall back to keyword search.</li>
<li><strong>Database hang:</strong> Long-running query. Check query plan with EXPLAIN ANALYZE. Add indexes if needed.</li>
<li><strong>Goroutine leak:</strong> goroutine count keeps growing. Use pprof to find leak.</li>
<li><strong>Network latency:</strong> Client far away, high packet loss. Add CDN or reduce payload size.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Monitoring in Production</h2>

<h3>Key Metrics to Track</h3>

<pre><code>// Using Prometheus
search_requests_total (counter)  // total requests since start
search_latency_seconds (histogram)  // p50, p95, p99
search_errors_total (counter)  // errors by type
active_search_requests (gauge)  // current in-flight
embedding_cache_hits_total (counter)  // cache efficacy
db_query_duration_seconds (histogram)  // database performance
</code></pre>

<h3>Alerting</h3>

<p>Set up alerts for production incidents:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>p99 latency > 500ms</strong> → investigate database or LLM</li>
<li><strong>Error rate > 1%</strong> → check logs for exceptions</li>
<li><strong>Memory growth > 2GB</strong> → possible goroutine leak</li>
<li><strong>Embedding cache hit rate < 50%</strong> → consider longer TTL</li>
</ul>

<h2>Code Path Reference: Detailed</h2>

<p>For full debugging, add tracing at each step:</p>

<pre><code>// handler/search.go - Add timing instrumentation
func (h *SearchHandler) Search(c *gin.Context) {
    start := time.Now()
    defer func() {
        elapsed := time.Since(start)
        logger.Info("search total", "ms", elapsed.Milliseconds())
        c.Header("X-Total-Time-Ms", fmt.Sprint(elapsed.Milliseconds()))
    }()
    
    // Step 1: Unmarshal (measure)
    t1 := time.Now()
    var req SearchRequest
    if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&req); err != nil {
        logger.Error("unmarshal failed", "ms", time.Since(t1).Milliseconds())
        return
    }
    logger.Info("unmarshal", "ms", time.Since(t1).Milliseconds())
    
    // Step 2: Call service (measure)
    t2 := time.Now()
    result, err := h.searchService.Search(c.Request.Context(), &req)
    logger.Info("service", "ms", time.Since(t2).Milliseconds())
    
    // Step 3: Marshal response (measure)
    t3 := time.Now()
    c.JSON(200, result)
    logger.Info("marshal", "ms", time.Since(t3).Milliseconds())
}
</code></pre>


